            <div xml:id="d788">

                <pb facs="0899" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.404/179½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Mexican
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-23">September 23, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On July 16, 1935, the President received at the White House a delegation of
                    Congressmen who presented a petition in connection with alleged religious
                    persecutions in Mexico.</p>
                <p>At the conclusion of this interview the President authorized the following
                    statement: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“That he is in entire sympathy with all people who make it clear that the
                            American people and Government believe in freedom of religious worship,
                            not only in the United States but also in other nations.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward L. Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
